{"overview":{"Symbol":"YSWY","Name":"Yesway, Inc.","Description":"Yesway, Inc. owns and operates convenience stores in the United States. The company's store offers packaged bakery items, bottled water, salty snacks, bagged candy, jerky, chips, milk, bread, eggs, packaged beverages, meat snacks, chocolate, and nuts. It also offers food services, including deep-fried burritos. In addition, its store offers other ancillary services, including cash ATMs, crypto-currency ATMs, money orders, gift cards, propane tanks, in-store gaming, Amazon Lockers, lottery tickets, and other non-consumable products. It operates under two brands: Yesway and Allsup's. The company was founded in 2015 and is based in Fort Worth, Texas.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NasdaqGS","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Consumer Defensive","Industry":"Grocery Stores","Address":"2301 Eagle Parkway, Fort Worth, TX, 76177, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"1567861504","EBITDA":"214735008","PERatio":"","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"","DividendPerShare":"","DividendYield":"","EPS":"-1.24","RevenuePerShareTTM":"","ProfitMargin":"0.03266","OperatingMarginTTM":"0.06925","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"","RevenueTTM":"2751228928","GrossProfitTTM":"595828992","DilutedEPSTTM":"-1.24","QuarterlyEarningsGrowthYOY":"","QuarterlyRevenueGrowthYOY":"0.144","AnalystTargetPrice":"29.125","TrailingPE":"","ForwardPE":"23.73731","PriceToSalesRatioTTM":"0.5698768","PriceToBookRatio":"","EVToRevenue":"0.604","EVToEBITDA":"7.74","Beta":"","52WeekHigh":"29.08","52WeekLow":"19.61","50DayMovingAverage":"23.934","200DayMovingAverage":"23.934","SharesOutstanding":"31185562","DividendDate":"","ExDividendDate":"","DebtToEquity":"163.592"},"daily":{"Meta Data":{"1. Information":"Daily Time Series (Yahoo Finance, shaped like Alpha Vantage)","2. Symbol":"YSWY","3. Last Refreshed":"2026-10-30","4. Output Size":"Compact"},"Time Series (Daily)":{"2026-04-22":{"1. open":"22","2